Chapter: DeskRootGuardTest
  cites Works chapter GopDesk

 Pins the decision `desk-root-reclaim` makes, which is WORKS-59: a mark records
 where a pane's state STARTED, the Browser rebuilds its state elsewhere on
 re-entry, and a mark left behind describes an address the state no longer
 occupies. The reclaim then freed live memory and the next re-entry ran through
 it, halting the guest. `desk-marks-remark` is the other half and this arm
 cannot see it; what this pins is that a live mark AT the root's end blocks the
 reclaim, which is the state remarking produces.

 The fixture is four mark stacks built by hand, for the reason `desk-span`
 gives: these are stacks the desk cannot be made to produce on demand.

Section: Fixture

 A root that starts at 1000 and ends at 2000.

  root-start : Integer = 1000
  root-end : Integer = 2000

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let ms-quiet = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let ms-live = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let p1 = desk-marks-push ms-live desk-focus-files 3000
    in let ms-at = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let p3 = desk-marks-push ms-at desk-focus-bro root-end
    in let ms-low = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let p2 = desk-marks-push ms-low desk-focus-files 500
    in act
    print-line-uni ("settled: " & dk-yn (desk-root-may-reclaim ms-quiet root-start root-end))
    print-line-uni ("live-at-e: " & dk-yn (desk-root-may-reclaim ms-at root-start root-end))
    print-line-uni ("live-above: " & dk-yn (desk-root-may-reclaim ms-live root-start root-end))
    print-line-uni ("live-below: " & dk-yn (desk-root-may-reclaim ms-low root-start root-end))
    print-line-uni ("unwritten: " & dk-yn (desk-root-may-reclaim ms-quiet 0 root-end) & " " & dk-yn (desk-root-may-reclaim ms-quiet root-start 0))
  end
